    By how many bytes the program grew while *input*, the bytes of one
    request or of several as a client would send them, was played to *app*
    *times* times, each over a fresh in-memory connection. Before that it is
    played *warm* times without being counted, so that what is allocated
    once and kept (a buffer that grows to its size, a list that reaches its
    length) is not taken for a leak.
